.Dd November 21, 2026
.Dt JOBMARSHAL-WRAPPER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jobmarshal-wrapper
.Nd execute commands within a shared native job budget
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
transparently executes a command on Linux and FreeBSD.
The
.Cm run
command of
.Xr jobmarshal 1
provides explicit execution through this wrapper without requiring aliases.
It preserves arguments, environment, working directory, standard streams,
exit status, and signals by replacing itself with the command.
.Pp
For independent builds, the wrapper starts the per-user
.Xr jobmarshal 1
service if necessary and reserves one token for the build's implicit slot.
It advertises the remaining native FIFO budget through
.Ev CARGO_MAKEFLAGS ,
.Ev MAKEFLAGS ,
and
.Ev MFLAGS
while preserving unrelated flags.
The build lease and participation lock survive execution in descendants.
The reserved token returns when the final lease descriptor closes.
.Pp
A valid inherited GNU or Cargo jobserver allocation is reused without a new
reservation, including nested builds with a capacity of one.
Environment selection follows the native library's precedence:
.Ev CARGO_MAKEFLAGS ,
.Ev MAKEFLAGS ,
then
.Ev MFLAGS .
Flags without authentication allow independent admission; invalid advertised
authentication fails without running the command.
.Pp
When invoked through a hardlink with another basename, the wrapper searches
.Ev PATH
for its own device and inode, skips all its aliases, and executes the next
executable with that basename.
For configure-installed aliases, the management command must be at that PATH
anchor.  Managed per-user aliases locate the management command through PATH.
In direct mode, a sibling development
.Nm jobmarshal
is preferred; otherwise it is found through PATH.
.Pp
Stopping the service rejects queued and new independent builds, lets active and
nested work finish, and waits for all leases and responses before teardown.
Surviving participants prevent a new pool after a daemon crash.
Lost native tokens remain unavailable until a safe stop and restart.
.Sh INSTALLATION
Prefer the per-user management commands:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
jobmarshal add-wrapper cargo
jobmarshal add-wrapper cc
eval "$(jobmarshal start)"
.Ed
.Pp
Aliases in $XDG_DATA_HOME/jobmarshal/bin are hardlinks to a private user-owned
copy in $XDG_DATA_HOME/jobmarshal/libexec/jobmarshal-wrapper, falling back to copies
when hardlinks are unavailable.
The data base defaults to $HOME/.local/share.
Keep the installed jobmarshal command in PATH for autostart.
New daemon launches refresh the private copy and stale aliases; starting an
existing daemon skips refresh.
See
.Xr jobmarshal 1
for listing, removal, storage rules, and error behavior.
.Pp
Alternatively, configure selects the complete set of installed command basenames with
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\&./configure --enable-wrappers='cargo cc mold'
.Ed
.Pp
The default and
.Fl -disable-wrappers
install no aliases.
Names must begin with an ASCII letter or digit and contain only ASCII letters,
digits, underscores, periods, plus signs, or hyphens.
The names
.Nm jobmarshal
and
.Nm jobmarshal-wrapper
are reserved.
Duplicate names are removed and the selection is sorted.
Bare
.Fl -enable-wrappers
requires a value and fails.
.Pp
Aliases are hardlinks from bindir to the wrapper in libexecdir.
Both directories must support hardlinks on the same filesystem.
No symlinks or installed link manifest are used.
Put bindir before the real command locations in
.Ev PATH .
Installation refuses unrelated files and symlinks at alias destinations.
Reinstalling the same selection is safe; uninstall preserves unrelated replacements.
Before changing the selection, uninstall with the original configuration and
directory settings, then reconfigure and reinstall.
.Pp
.Cm jobmarshal run
finds this wrapper at
.Pa ../libexec/jobmarshal-wrapper
relative to the management executable.
Preserve this layout when customizing directories or relocating an installation.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width JOBMARSHAL_RUNTIME_DIR
.It Ev JOBMARSHAL_RUNTIME_DIR
Private runtime-directory override; see
.Xr jobmarshal 1 .
.It Ev JOBMARSHAL_JOBS
Requested capacity when autostarting the service.
.It Ev CARGO_MAKEFLAGS , MAKEFLAGS , MFLAGS
Inherited native jobserver authentication and preserved build flags.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Successfully executed commands retain their exit status or signal.
Wrapper setup or execution errors return 125 and print diagnostics to standard
error without executing an uncoordinated command.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jobmarshal 1
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/jmmv/jobmarshal
